---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="EMG Biopotential Signal Processing and Actuator Control" sideBarActiveItemID="projects">

  <div class="mb-4">
    <a href="/projects" class="text-sm hover:underline flex items-center gap-1">
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <path d="m15 18-6-6 6-6"/>
      </svg>
      Back to Projects
    </a>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-8">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-4">EMG Biopotential Signal Processing and Actuator Control</h1>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-6">
      <span class="border border-current px-2 py-0.5 text-xs text-black dark:text-white rounded">Biomedical</span>
      <span class="border border-current px-2 py-0.5 text-xs text-black dark:text-white rounded">Signal Processing</span>
      <span class="border border-current px-2 py-0.5 text-xs text-black dark:text-white rounded">Embedded</span>
      <span class="bg-gray-800 text-white dark:bg-gray-200 dark:text-black px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold rounded">COURSE PROJECT</span>
    </div>

    <!-- Metadata Normal Paragraphs -->
    <div class="text-lg mb-8 text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200">
      <p class="mb-2"><strong>Course:</strong> TF3214 Biomedical Instrumentation and Control, ITB</p>
      <p class="mb-2"><strong>Team:</strong> Dika Muhammad Azis, Umar Abdurrahman</p>
      <p class="mb-2"><strong>Tech Stack:</strong> MATLAB, ESP32, Arduino IDE, SPIFFS</p>
      <p class="mb-2"><strong>Source:</strong> <a href="https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/13jZwUaNJ561s1cvyHIG9nNgAKnIEb79j" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-semibold">View GDrive ↗</a></p>
    </div>

    <!-- Hero Image (replaces the video section) -->
    <div class="mt-12 mb-12">
      <div class="w-full md:w-3/4 lg:w-1/2">
        <img src="/projects/emg/emg1.png" alt="Surface EMG electrodes on the biceps during relaxed and contracted states" class="w-full rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div>
      <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
        Electromyography (EMG) records the electrical activity of muscle fibers when a muscle contracts or relaxes. This project covers the full chain from a raw biceps EMG recording to a simple ON/OFF actuator command: identifying signal and noise characteristics, designing digital filters, and driving an LED from the cleaned signal.
      </p>

      <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
        The raw recording was analyzed in MATLAB in both the time domain and the power spectral domain, then cleaned with a high-pass filter and a notch filter. The cleaned amplitude was exported to an ESP32, which turns an LED on during muscle movement and off at rest.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3 mt-8">Signal Analysis & Filtering</h3>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
        <li><strong>Sampling:</strong> 500 Hz, chosen so the signal duration matches the 200 s reference recording.</li>
        <li><strong>Time-domain features:</strong> IEMG, MAV, RMS, SSI and WL.</li>
        <li><strong>Frequency-domain features:</strong> MNF, MDF, MNP, PKF and TTP, estimated with Welch's method (1024-point segments, Hamming window).</li>
        <li><strong>Noise identified:</strong> DC offset around 500, 50 Hz mains interference with harmonics at 100, 150 and 200 Hz, and low-frequency movement artifacts (about 0–15 Hz).</li>
        <li><strong>Filtering:</strong> 8th-order high-pass IIR at 20 Hz plus notch filters at 50, 100, 150 and 200 Hz (Q = 35), applied with <code>filtfilt</code> for zero-phase output.</li>
        <li><strong>Result:</strong> The power spectrum after filtering shows the low-frequency content suppressed and deep notches at the mains harmonics, leaving most EMG energy between roughly 20 and 150 Hz.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3 mt-8">Actuator Control</h3>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
        <li><strong>Feature used:</strong> Absolute time-domain amplitude of the filtered signal.</li>
        <li><strong>Data path:</strong> Filtered data exported from MATLAB as a .txt file (about 1.8 MB), stored in the ESP32 SPIFFS memory and replayed at 500 Hz (one sample every 2 ms).</li>
        <li><strong>Threshold:</strong> Amplitude above 35 (the largest value seen at rest) drives GPIO 25 to 3.3 V and lights the LED; otherwise the LED stays off.</li>
        <li><strong>Circuit:</strong> GPIO 25 → 1.2 kΩ resistor → red LED on a breadboard, about 1.3 mA through the LED.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Image Gallery Slider -->
  <div class="mt-12">
    <h3 class="text-3xl w-full font-bold mb-6">Gallery</h3>

    <!-- Slider Container -->
    <div class="flex overflow-x-auto snap-x snap-mandatory gap-4 pb-6 custom-scrollbar">
      <div class="snap-start shrink-0 w-[80vw] sm:w-[45vw] md:w-[350px] lg:w-[450px]">
        <img src="/projects/emg/emg2.png" alt="Raw EMG signal in the time domain" class="w-full h-48 md:h-[280px] object-cover rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <div class="snap-start shrink-0 w-[80vw] sm:w-[45vw] md:w-[350px] lg:w-[450px]">
        <img src="/projects/emg/emg3.png" alt="Power spectral density before and after filtering" class="w-full h-48 md:h-[280px] object-cover rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <div class="snap-start shrink-0 w-[80vw] sm:w-[45vw] md:w-[350px] lg:w-[450px]">
        <img src="/projects/emg/emg4.png" alt="MATLAB signal processing flowchart" class="w-full h-48 md:h-[280px] object-cover rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <div class="snap-start shrink-0 w-[80vw] sm:w-[45vw] md:w-[350px] lg:w-[450px]">
        <img src="/projects/emg/emg5.png" alt="ESP32 and LED breadboard setup" class="w-full h-48 md:h-[280px] object-cover rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <div class="snap-start shrink-0 w-[80vw] sm:w-[45vw] md:w-[350px] lg:w-[450px]">
        <img src="/projects/emg/emg6.png" alt="ESP32 actuator control flowchart" class="w-full h-48 md:h-[280px] object-cover rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <div class="snap-start shrink-0 w-[80vw] sm:w-[45vw] md:w-[350px] lg:w-[450px]">
        <img src="/projects/emg/emg7.png" alt="ESP32 wiring diagram with resistor and LED" class="w-full h-48 md:h-[280px] object-contain bg-white rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Custom Scrollbar for the Gallery Slider */
  .custom-scrollbar::-webkit-scrollbar {
    height: 10px;
  }
  .custom-scrollbar::-webkit-scrollbar-track {
    background: #e5e7eb;
    border-radius: 8px;
  }
  .custom-scrollbar::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {
    background: #9ca3af;
    border-radius: 8px;
  }
  .custom-scrollbar::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:hover {
    background: #6b7280;
  }
  /* Dark mode scrollbar */
  :global(.dark) .custom-scrollbar::-webkit-scrollbar-track {
    background: #374151;
  }
  :global(.dark) .custom-scrollbar::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {
    background: #6b7280;
  }
  :global(.dark) .custom-scrollbar::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:hover {
    background: #9ca3af;
  }
</style>